.\" robodr-diode-pack(1). Source of truth: the USAGE text in
.\" crates/robodr-diode/src/bin/robodr-diode-pack.rs and the crate README.
.\" Keep them in sync.
.TH ROBODR\-DIODE\-PACK 1 "2026-10-16" "RoboDR 0.1.0-alpha.1" "RoboDR Manual"
.SH NAME
robodr\-diode\-pack \- pack RoboDR findings and black\-box bundles into signed batches for one\-way export
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B robodr\-diode\-pack
.B \-\-outbox
.I DIR
.B \-\-state
.I FILE
.B \-\-unit
.I UNIT_ID
.B \-\-key\-file
.I SECRET_KEY_FILE
.RB [ \-\-key\-id
.IR KEY_ID ]
.RB [ \-\-allow\-hmac ]
.RB [ \-\-findings
.IR FINDINGS.jsonl ]...
.RB [ \-\-bundle
.IR BUNDLE.rbbx ]...
.RB [ \-\-max\-batch\-bytes
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-max\-findings
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-now\-ms
.IR MS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Low\-side (air\-gapped) packer of the RoboDR one\-way export
.RI ( robodr\-diode/1 ).
It validates every finding (OCSF contract) and every black\-box export bundle,
then writes signed, sequence\-numbered batch directories
.RI ( rdd_ UNIT _ SEQ )
into
.IR DIR .
Batches are staged in dot\-directories and published by an atomic rename:
.B the transfer agent must ignore dot\-entries.
Any invalid input aborts before anything is written. The published batches are
printed as JSON. There is no network code; a diode transfer agent or a person
with media moves the batches.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-outbox " DIR"
Output directory (a symlinked outbox is refused).
.TP
.BI \-\-state " FILE"
Packer state (next sequence number, last batch hash), committed atomically.
.TP
.BI \-\-unit " UNIT_ID"
Unit id written into every manifest.
.TP
.BI \-\-key\-file " SECRET_KEY_FILE"
The unit's signing key: a
.BR robodr\-blackbox (1)
secret key file, Ed25519 by default
.RB ( "robodr\-blackbox keygen" ).
It is refused if it is a symlink or not a regular file, if group or others
can access it, or if it is owned by neither the current user nor root.
Public key files and bare hex keys are refused. Keys are never taken on the
command line.
.TP
.BI \-\-key\-id " KEY_ID"
Optional; must equal the key file's id.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-hmac
Accept a legacy HMAC\-SHA256 key file (refused otherwise). A warning is
printed: with HMAC the receiving side holds the same secret and could forge
batches.
.TP
.BI \-\-findings " FINDINGS.jsonl"
Findings to export, one JSON value per line (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-bundle " BUNDLE.rbbx"
Black\-box export bundle to export (repeatable).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-batch\-bytes " N"
Data per batch, 64 KiB + 1 to 1 GiB (default 16 MiB).
.TP
.BI \-\-max\-findings " N"
Findings per batch, at least 1 (default 10000).
.TP
.BI \-\-now\-ms " MS"
Creation time (Unix ms) written into the manifests; default: now.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (invalid input, key, I/O).
.TP
.B 2
Usage error, including an argument that is not valid UTF\-8.
.SH NOTES
Give the SOC only the public key file
.RI ( SECRET_KEY_FILE .pub,
or
.BR "robodr\-blackbox export\-pub" ).
The Ed25519 implementation is in\-crate and not audited.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR robodr\-diode\-unpack (1),
.BR robodr\-blackbox (1),
/usr/share/doc/robodr/OPERATIONS.md
